Project Team, Finance, Professor Wang:

Your JICA Technical Cooperation Project grant installment
of JPY 42,000,000 is ready for disbursement.

Project Details:
  Project Number: JPN-C-8842
  Title: Adaptive Email Threat Detection
  Scheme: Technical Cooperation (TCP) FY2024
  Japan Partner: NICT
  China Partner: Your Company + Zhejiang University
  Total Grant: JPY 168,000,000 (3 years)
  Current Installment: Year 3 Q1 — JPY 42,000,000

Disbursement Process:

  1. JICA will send the disbursement verification form
     by REGISTERED MAIL to your company's registered
     address in China

  2. Complete the form and return by mail with:
     — Banking information (on JICA's official form)
     — Company registration certificate
     — Certified English translation

  3. JICA processes disbursement within 15 business days
     of receiving completed forms

  Important Security Notes:
  JICA will NEVER:
  - Send direct banking verification links via email
  - Require Google Workspace authentication for grant
    disbursement
  - Request offline_access or OAuth permissions
  - Ask for passport copies through email portals
  - Offer a "Chinese portal channel" for banking
  - Cite "FEFTA compliance" to require online banking
    re-verification
  - Set a "November 14 deadline" for banking verification
    (grants are held, not lost, pending verification)

  JICA's actual disbursement process:
  — Banking information on PAPER FORMS sent by
     REGISTERED MAIL to your China address
  — No online portal exists for banking verification
  — JICA has NOT implemented Google Workspace federated
     login for grant management
  — Unclaimed grants are held in the project budget,
     not lost or re-allocated without notification

  If you receive an email with a "Verify Banking" button
  or Google Workspace OAuth, it is a phishing attempt
  targeting JICA grant recipients.

